	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "M.2 Key-B SMD socket (host-PCB receptacle), LOTES APCI0105-P001A, LCSC C841658, 67-pin (75-position, B-key notch removes 12-19), 0.5mm pitch, H4.2. GEOMETRY REPLACED Task 14b: pad geometry taken verbatim from the LCSC/EasyEDA C841658 footprint (easyeda2kicad --full), the land pattern JLCPCB physically assembles this socket against. Two gull-wing rows at y=+/-3.77mm (7.54mm row separation), signal pads 0.30x1.55mm, plus 2 mechanical solder tabs (pads 76/77, 1.2x2.75mm at x=+/-10.35) and 2 unnumbered locating-peg holes at x=+/-10.0. Replaces the Task-14 approximation whose two rows sat 0.8mm apart on the SAME side of the connector (overlapping copper/mask), with 0.25x1.1mm pads and X-mirrored pin order -- see docs/footprint-verification.md.")
